From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Micheal Waltz <micheal@ecliptik.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 15:15:26 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 5/7] psDooM: processes as monsters, through libpsd

The hooks psDooM 2000.05.03.b added to XDoom, on linuxdoom-1.10. The
logic lives in psdoom/p_psdoom.c (psdoom-plus tree) and libpsd; this
patch only calls it:

- p_mobj.h, r_defs.h: pid, label and flags on things and vissprites
- d_main.c: auto-load psdoom1/2.wad (unless -nopslev), open libpsd
- p_setup.c: forget the old level's monsters, spawn processes on load
- p_tick.c: poll processes every tic (libpsd decides how often to look)
- p_inter.c: only players hurt pid monsters (-nopssafety lifts it);
  damage renices, death kills, a vanished process drops nothing
- p_mobj.c: tell libpsd when the engine removes a pid monster;
  -respawnitems (psDooM)
- p_saveg.c: pid monsters aren't saved; resync after loading
- g_game.c: -nomonsters. persists across new games (psDooM)
- r_things.c: psDooM's floating 'pid / name' label above each monster
---
